menu "NAND UBI configuration"

    config ESP_NAND_UBI_ENABLE
        bool "Enable UBI-like layer for SPI NAND flash"
        depends on NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_BDL
        default n
        help
            Enables the esp_nand_ubi component. Requires CONFIG_NAND_FLASH_ENABLE_BDL
            and ESP-IDF >= 6.0. Provides position-independent factory images and
            bad-block hiding on SPI NAND flash by exposing a flat logical-erase-block
            (LEB) address space per volume above the raw NAND block device.

    config ESP_NAND_UBI_RESERVED_PEBS
        int "Default number of reserved PEBs for bad-block pool"
        depends on ESP_NAND_UBI_ENABLE
        range 0 32
        default 4
        help
            Number of physical erase blocks held back as a spare pool for bad-block
            replacement. Used as the default when nand_ubi_config_t.reserved_pebs is
            not overridden by the caller.

    config ESP_NAND_UBI_ALLOC_SAMPLES
        int "Free PEBs sampled per allocation"
        depends on ESP_NAND_UBI_ENABLE
        range 1 8
        default 4
        help
            Each allocation reads the EC headers of this many randomly chosen free PEBs
            and takes the one with the lowest erase count. Erase counts are not kept in
            RAM. 1 picks a random free PEB with no wear leveling; 2 or more keep the
            erase-count spread bounded, and larger values narrow it further at the cost
            of one EC header read per extra sample.


    config ESP_NAND_UBI_CHECKPOINT
        bool "Attach checkpoint (fast attach)"
        depends on ESP_NAND_UBI_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            Keeps a snapshot of the LEB map and PEB states on flash, so attach reads the
            snapshot and a small set of PEBs instead of every PEB. Reserves a region at
            the start of the chip for the snapshot; erased LEBs keep their PEB until the
            next snapshot is written. A chip with checkpoints still attaches by full scan,
            also on Linux. See docs/fastmap-design.md.

            A volume created with this option off may reserve more LEBs than fit outside
            the region; attach then warns, and writes fail once the chip is full.

    config ESP_NAND_UBI_CKPT_REGION_PEBS
        int "Checkpoint region size in PEBs (0 = square root of the PEB count)"
        depends on ESP_NAND_UBI_CHECKPOINT
        range 0 1024
        default 0

    config ESP_NAND_UBI_CKPT_POOL_PEBS
        int "Free PEBs per checkpoint (0 = region size)"
        depends on ESP_NAND_UBI_CHECKPOINT
        range 0 1024
        default 0
        help
            Writes go to these PEBs between two checkpoints. A larger pool writes
            checkpoints less often, but attach reads more PEBs and the write that
            refills the pool takes longer.

endmenu
